---
import { sitePath } from '../lib/paths';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Opportunities" description="Student and collaboration inquiries for the Climate Resilient and Equitable Infrastructure Lab.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap join">
      <h1>Join Us</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We welcome applicants motivated to address challenges at the intersection of climate change,
        resilient infrastructure, and environmental justice. Our research studies how critical
        infrastructure (e.g., levees, dams, slopes) withstands and adapts to extreme events (e.g.,
        drought, flooding, wildfires, compound and cascading hazards) in a changing climate. Our work
        combines systems engineering with geotechnical modeling, environmental science, remote
        sensing, and data-driven computational methods.
      </p>

      <h2>Prospective Students</h2>
      <p>
        We encourage applicants to explore our <a href={sitePath('/projects')}>projects</a> and
        <a href={sitePath('/publications')}>publications</a> to learn more about our research.
        Interested students should contact Dr. Vahedifard at
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Prospective Student: [Last Name]')}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
        with the subject line “Prospective Student: [Last Name]”, a CV, and a brief introduction
        outlining (1) your motivation for joining the group and (2) the research questions or topics
        that excite you most. Please check the relevant Tufts department or graduate program website
        for application requirements and deadlines.
      </p>

      <h2>Research Collaboration</h2>
      <p>
        We actively collaborate with researchers across disciplines and around the world, as well as
        with agencies and practitioners. To discuss a potential collaboration, please email
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>Dr. Vahedifard</a> with a brief description of your research
        question and how it connects with our work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* One comfortable reading column; sections separated by a hairline, not just space. */
  .join {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .join h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4, 1.25rem);
  }

  .join .lede {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .join h2 {
    margin: var(--space-6, 2.5rem) 0 var(--space-3, 0.75rem);
    padding-top: var(--space-5, 1.75rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  .join p:not(.lede) {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
